DATASET DESCRIPTION
The Google Play Store dataset contains information about mobile applications available on the Google Play Store. It is commonly used for data analysis, visualization, and machine learning projects to understand app popularity, ratings, pricing, and categories.

Number of rows (apps): 10,841

Number of columns (features): 13

The dataset contains 13 key columns that categorize and quantify mobile applications on the Google Play Store. It includes basic identifying information like the App name and Category, alongside performance metrics such as Rating, number of Reviews, and total Installs. Technical details are captured in the Size, Current Ver, and Android Ver (minimum OS requirement) columns, while commercial attributes are defined by Type (Free/Paid) and Price. Finally, the dataset provides contextual metadata through Content Rating (age suitability), Genres (sub-categories), and the Last Updated date to track software recency.
